# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Audiobooks ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your audiobooks library. Anything
# you put here gets silently dropped from output/audiobooks/warnings.json on
# every run.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy this file to `ignored/audiobooks.yaml` (drop the `.example`
#      suffix). The real `audiobooks.yaml` is gitignored so your personal
#      decisions don't end up in version control.
#   2. Add path prefixes below — one per line.
#   3. Re-run `npm run audiobooks`. Matching warnings disappear from output.
#
# How matching works: each entry is a path PREFIX. A warning whose `path`
# starts with one of these (slash- or end-of-string-bounded) is silenced.
# Matching is case-insensitive and forward-slash-normalized, so it works on
# Windows and macOS/Linux libraries alike.
#
# Get the paths to add from output/audiobooks/warnings.json. Most audiobook
# warnings use the `<Author>/<Book>` path shape.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence one book
# (Drops every warning under this book's folder. Useful for a book with
# known missing chapters or chapter naming you've decided to keep.)
# - J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings
# - Terry Pratchett/Discworld 41


# Silence a whole category folder
# (Drops EVERY warning under this folder.)
# - Other Audible
# - Book On CD


# Silence a whole author
# (Rare — usually only useful when one author's catalog has the same
# recurring issue across every book.)
# - Some Author
